        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by a silent data-loss issue during the merging of segments in the Lucene index. Specifically, when segments being merged had non-congruent field numbers (i.e., the same field name mapped to different field numbers), binary fields could be truncated to 0 bytes instead of retaining their original data, leading to potential data loss.

